---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const pageTitle = "Privacy Policy | IsItKitchenSafe";
const pageDescription = "Read the Privacy Policy for IsItKitchenSafe. Learn how we collect traffic data, cookies, comply with GDPR, CCPA/CPRA, and handle third-party advertising guidelines.";

const privacyFaqs = [
  {
    question: "Does IsItKitchenSafe collect personal data?",
    answer: "We do not collect personal data from casual browsing. Standard server log files and Google AdSense advertising cookies are used to analyze traffic and serve relevant ads."
  },
  {
    question: "How can I opt out of Google personalized advertising cookies?",
    answer: "You can opt out of Google's personalized advertising by visiting Google Ads Settings (https://adssettings.google.com/) or via the Digital Advertising Alliance at https://www.aboutads.info/choices/."
  },
  {
    question: "How does IsItKitchenSafe comply with GDPR and CCPA/CPRA?",
    answer: "We provide an explicit cookie consent mechanism, honor Global Privacy Control (GPC) signals, never sell user personal data, and allow users to opt out of cross-context behavioral advertising at any time."
  }
];
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} faqs={privacyFaqs} excludeArticleSchema={true} availableLocales={['en', 'es', 'pt', 'zh-cn', 'ja']}>
  <section class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6 py-[96px]">
    <h1 class="text-display-lg font-medium text-ink tracking-tight mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>
    
    <div class="prose max-w-none text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed flex flex-col gap-6">
      <p class="text-muted text-[13px]">Last updated: October 23, 2026</p>

      <p>
        At <strong>Is It Kitchen Safe?</strong> (accessible from isitkitchensafe.com), the privacy of our visitors is of paramount importance to us. This Privacy Policy document outlines the types of information received, recorded, and collected by our website and explains how that information is utilized in accordance with global privacy regulations including GDPR, CCPA/CPRA, and Google AdSense publisher policies.
      </p>

      <div class="border-t border-hairline my-4"></div>

      <h2 class="text-title-lg text-ink font-medium tracking-tight">1. Server Log Files</h2>
      <p>
        Like most standard websites, isitkitchensafe.com utilizes server log files. Information recorded inside log files includes internet protocol (IP) addresses, browser type, Internet Service Provider (ISP), date/time stamps, referring and exit pages, platform type, and number of clicks. This data is utilized strictly to analyze trends, administer the site, track anonymous user aggregate movements across the site, and gather broad demographic data. IP addresses and log data are not linked to any information that is personally identifiable.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-title-lg text-ink font-medium tracking-tight">2. Cookies, Web Beacons & Consent Management</h2>
      <p>
        We use cookies to store information about visitors' preferences, record user-specific information on which pages are accessed, and customize content based on browser type. We deploy a Cookie Consent banner that allows users to accept or decline non-essential cookies. We implement Google Consent Mode v2 and support the IAB Europe Transparency and Consent Framework (TCF v2.2) to communicate user privacy choices to downstream technology partners.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-title-lg text-ink font-medium tracking-tight">3. Google AdSense & Third-Party Advertising Disclosures</h2>
      <p>
        Google is an authorized third-party vendor on isitkitchensafe.com. Google uses cookies (including the DoubleClick / DART cookie and interest-based identifiers) to serve advertisements to visitors based upon their visits to this site and other sites across the internet:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2">
        <li>
          Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to our website or other websites on the internet.
        </li>
        <li>
          Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to our users based on their visit to our site and/or other sites on the Internet.
        </li>
        <li>
          Users may opt out of personalized advertising at any time by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">Google Ads Settings</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Alternatively, users can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting the <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">Network Advertising Initiative / AboutAds Opt-Out Page</a> or <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">NAI Consumer Opt-Out</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Visitors residing in the European Union or United Kingdom may also manage and opt out of advertising cookies via <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">Your Online Choices</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Third-party ad servers or ad networks use technology in their advertisements and links appearing on isitkitchensafe.com to transmit directly to your browser, automatically receiving your IP address. They may also employ JavaScript, web beacons, and cookies to evaluate the effectiveness of their advertising campaigns and personalize ad content. <strong>Is It Kitchen Safe?</strong> has no access to or control over cookies used by third-party advertisers.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-title-lg text-ink font-medium tracking-tight">4. CCPA / CPRA Notice (California Consumer Privacy Act)</h2>
      <p>
        Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), California residents have specific privacy rights regarding their personal information:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2">
        <li><strong>Right to Know / Access:</strong> The right to request disclosure of the categories and specific pieces of personal information collected about you over the past 12 months.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Deletion:</strong> The right to request the deletion of personal information collected from you, subject to legal exceptions.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Correction:</strong> The right to request correction of inaccurate personal information.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Opt-Out of Sale or Sharing ("Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information"):</strong> We do not sell personal information for monetary consideration. However, the use of third-party advertising cookies may be classified as "sharing" for cross-context behavioral advertising under California law. You may opt out of cross-context behavioral advertising by using our cookie consent controls, enabling the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal in your browser, or visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link underline">AboutAds Choices</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Non-Discrimination:</strong> We will never discriminate against you for exercising any of your CCPA/CPRA rights.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-title-lg text-ink font-medium tracking-tight">5. GDPR & EEA / UK Data Subject Rights</h2>
      <p>
        If you are a resident of the European Economic Area (EEA) or the United Kingdom, you possess specific data protection rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and UK GDPR:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-1.5">
        <li><strong>Legal Basis for Processing:</strong> We process data based on your explicit consent (for non-essential cookies and targeted advertising) or our legitimate interests in operating, securing, and maintaining an educational safety resource.</li>
        <li><strong>Right of Access, Rectification & Erasure:</strong> You may request copies of your personal data, request corrections, or request erasure of stored records.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Restrict or Object to Processing:</strong> You have the right to object to or restrict processing of your personal data at any time.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Data Portability:</strong> You may request transfer of collected data to another organization or directly to you in a structured format.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Withdraw Consent:</strong> You may withdraw your cookie or advertising consent at any time without penalty.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-title-lg text-ink font-medium tracking-tight">6. Children's Online Privacy Protection (COPPA)</h2>
      <p>
        Protecting the privacy of young children is especially important. isitkitchensafe.com does not knowingly collect any personally identifiable information from children under the age of 13. If a parent or guardian believes that our site possesses personally identifiable information of a child under 13 in its database, please contact us immediately and we will promptly remove such information from our records.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-title-lg text-ink font-medium tracking-tight">7. Data Retention & Security</h2>
      <p>
        We retain technical server log data for security and performance analysis for a maximum period of 24 months, after which it is permanently purged. We apply industry-standard HTTPS encryption (TLS 1.3), Content Security Policies, and HSTS headers across all endpoints to prevent interception or tampering.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-title-lg text-ink font-medium tracking-tight">8. Contact Information & Privacy Requests</h2>
      <p>
        For inquiries regarding this Privacy Policy, CCPA/CPRA requests, GDPR data rights, or general data handling questions, please contact our Data Privacy Officer via email at <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:privacy@isitkitchensafe.com" class="text-link hover:underline">privacy@isitkitchensafe.com</a><!--/email_off--> or <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:support@isitkitchensafe.com" class="text-link hover:underline">support@isitkitchensafe.com</a><!--/email_off-->.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
